# Original tier-badge screenshots (1284x2778 phone captures, ~2.7 MB each).
# The optimised, background-removed versions the site actually uses are
# committed at assets/warranty-*.png (~25 KB each). Keeping the raw captures
# out avoids ~8 MB sitting in git history forever. Delete these lines if you
# want the originals versioned too.
SureSkyEssential.png
SureSkyPlus.png
SureSkyPremium.png

# Full-size page exports of the sample roof report (~1.9 MB for the seven).
# The optimised copies the site serves are committed under
# assets/report-pages/ at ~450 KB total. Same reasoning as above.
/roof-report-sample-p*.png

# Original phone screenshots of the job photos (~8-9 MB each, all letterboxed).
# The cropped, compressed versions the site serves are committed under assets/
# at ~80-230 KB each. These source files get renamed as they are sorted, so the
# rule is a glob rather than a fixed list — nothing multi-megabyte at the root
# should reach the repo.
/Homes.png
/Shingles*.png
/CrewOnRoof.png
/HeroImage.png
/HomesHero.png
/HeroImage3.webp

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Dependencies (none today — the site is dependency-free)
node_modules/

# Local env / secrets — must never reach a public repo
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
